  "content_description": "",
  "content_text_body": "There may not realistically be enough resources to get everything done. Managers who think they can accomplish everything often end up getting very little done. The goal is to learn how to prioritize tasks for optimal productivity.\n\n ### Create a priority list\n\n Be clear about what should be done first, second, and third. As new items are added to your team's plate, communicate any impact the new item has on the priority list.\n\n ### Balance speed and quality\n\n Part of prioritizing is determining how quickly a task needs to be done, and the level of quality it requires. Quality can suffer when work is rushed, so for each task clearly communicate your expectations.\n\n ### Ask for advice\n\n Whom do you work with that is very good at prioritization, who almost always meets or beats deadlines? Ask them how they manage.",
